// test-error
// ADR-003 / #1306 review: the same answer with or without the header.
//
// With no include this used to report
//   E0422 ... hint: 'malloc' is available from stdlib.h -- try global.malloc()
// which directs the author to write the include the transpiler then rejects them
// for. The author's mistake does not change because a header is absent, so the
// code and the sentence do not change either.

void allocateMemory() {
    malloc(100);
}
